
---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Gardening | Silken Valley Lifestyle"
  description="Explore garden design, flowers, perennials, trees, shrubs, seasonal gardening, and practical garden care."
  heroTitle="Gardening"
  heroText="Garden inspiration, plant care, and beautiful outdoor living."
  heroCompact={true}
>
  <section class="hero garden-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Garden & Outdoor Living</p>
    <h1>Gardening & Landscape Inspiration</h1>
    <p>
      Discover the art and enjoyment of gardening through historic
      garden traditions, landscape design, flowering plants,
      seasonal inspiration, and practical horticultural knowledge.
      Whether creating a new garden or caring for an established
      landscape, find inspiration for making outdoor spaces beautiful
      and welcoming.
    </p>
  </section>

  <nav class="garden-nav" aria-label="Gardening page sections">
    <a href="#garden-design">Garden Design</a>
    <a href="#garden-history">Garden History</a>
    <a href="#flowers">Flowers & Perennials</a>
    <a href="#trees">Trees & Shrubs</a>
    <a href="#seasons">Seasonal Gardening</a>
    <a href="#garden-care">Garden Care</a>
  </nav>

  <section class="garden-section" id="garden-design">
    <p class="eyebrow">Planning Beautiful Outdoor Spaces</p>
    <h2>The Art of Garden Design</h2>
    <p>
      Garden design brings together architecture, horticulture,
      colour, texture, and the natural landscape. A thoughtfully
      designed garden creates a sense of harmony while providing
      spaces for relaxation, entertaining, and enjoying nature.
    </p>
    <p>
      Explore traditional and contemporary garden styles, from
      formal European landscapes and English cottage gardens to
      Mediterranean courtyards, naturalistic planting, and
      modern outdoor living spaces.
    </p>

    <div class="garden-feature-grid">
      <article class="garden-feature">
        <h3>Formal Gardens</h3>
        <p>
          Discover symmetry, geometric layouts, clipped hedges,
          parterres, fountains, and carefully arranged planting.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="garden-feature">
        <h3>Cottage Gardens</h3>
        <p>
          Explore abundant flowers, informal pathways, climbing
          roses, traditional perennials, and romantic planting.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="garden-feature">
        <h3>Mediterranean Gardens</h3>
        <p>
          Learn about stonework, courtyards, aromatic herbs,
          drought-conscious planting, and architectural evergreens.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="garden-feature">
        <h3>Naturalistic Gardens</h3>
        <p>
          Create relaxed landscapes with ornamental grasses,
          flowering perennials, native plants, and natural forms.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="garden-link">
      <a href="/gardening/garden-design/">Explore Garden Design →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="garden-section" id="garden-history">
    <p class="eyebrow">Gardens Through the Ages</p>
    <h2>The History & Inspiration of Gardens</h2>
    <p>
      Gardens have reflected the cultures, architecture, artistic
      traditions, and lifestyles of civilizations throughout history.
      From ancient Egyptian courtyards and Greek gardens to the
      elaborate landscapes of Renaissance Italy and formal gardens
      of Stuart and Georgian England, each period introduced
      distinctive ideas about outdoor spaces.
    </p>
    <p>
      Historical garden traditions continue to influence modern
      landscape design. Their use of symmetry, water, sculpture,
      planting arrangements, enclosed spaces, and garden rooms
      provides inspiration for contemporary gardens.
    </p>
    <ul class="garden-list">
      <li>Ancient Egyptian, Greek, Roman, and Persian gardens</li>
      <li>Renaissance Italian and Mediterranean landscapes</li>
      <li>Stuart and Georgian formal gardens</li>
      <li>English cottage and Victorian gardens</li>
      <li>Traditional European and modern landscape styles</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="garden-link">
      <a href="/gardening/garden-design/">Discover Historical Garden Design →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="garden-section" id="flowers">
    <p class="eyebrow">Colour, Fragrance & Planting</p>
    <h2>Flowers & Perennials</h2>
    <p>
      Flowers bring colour, fragrance, movement, and seasonal
      interest to the garden. Combining flowering shrubs,
      herbaceous perennials, annuals, bulbs, and ornamental grasses
      creates planting displays that evolve throughout the year.
    </p>
    <p>
      Learn about individual flower varieties, flowering periods,
      growing conditions, plant combinations, and the principles
      of creating beautiful perennial borders.
    </p>
    <p class="garden-link">
      <a href="/gardening/flowers/">Explore Flowers & Perennials →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="garden-section" id="trees">
    <p class="eyebrow">Structure & Year-Round Interest</p>
    <h2>Trees & Shrubs</h2>
    <p>
      Trees and shrubs provide the structure and framework of
      a successful landscape. They offer shade, privacy, seasonal
      flowers, foliage colour, interesting bark, and year-round
      garden interest.
    </p>
    <p>
      Explore ornamental trees, flowering shrubs, evergreen
      selections, hedging plants, and the considerations involved
      in choosing plants for different garden spaces.
    </p>
    <p class="garden-link">
      <a href="/gardening/trees-shrubs/">Explore Trees & Shrubs →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="garden-section" id="seasons">
    <p class="eyebrow">A Garden for Every Season</p>
    <h2>Seasonal Gardening</h2>
    <p>
      Gardening changes with the seasons. Planning throughout
      the year helps maintain healthy plants, encourage flowering,
      and keep outdoor spaces attractive and productive.
    </p>

    <div class="garden-feature-grid">
      <article class="garden-feature">
        <h3>Spring</h3>
        <p>
          Prepare garden beds, divide perennials, plant bulbs,
          prune appropriate shrubs, and begin seasonal planting.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="garden-feature">
        <h3>Summer</h3>
        <p>
          Maintain flowering borders, water thoughtfully,
          deadhead flowers, and enjoy the garden in full bloom.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="garden-feature">
        <h3>Autumn</h3>
        <p>
          Plant suitable trees and shrubs, collect seeds,
          prepare beds, and enjoy autumn foliage.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="garden-feature">
        <h3>Winter</h3>
        <p>
          Protect vulnerable plants, plan new garden projects,
          prune suitable dormant plants, and appreciate winter structure.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="garden-section" id="garden-care">
    <p class="eyebrow">Growing & Maintaining a Healthy Garden</p>
    <h2>Garden Care & Practical Advice</h2>
    <p>
      A beautiful garden begins with healthy soil, appropriate
      plant selection, and consistent care. Understanding the
      growing requirements of individual plants helps create
      stronger, healthier, and more resilient landscapes.
    </p>
    <ul class="garden-list">
      <li>Soil preparation and improvement</li>
      <li>Watering, drainage, and moisture management</li>
      <li>Pruning and seasonal maintenance</li>
      <li>Plant propagation and dividing perennials</li>
      <li>Mulching, composting, and soil health</li>
      <li>Garden planning and maintenance schedules</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="garden-link">
      <a href="/gardening/garden-care/">Explore Garden Care →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="garden-closing">
    <p class="eyebrow">Create Something Beautiful</p>
    <h2>Inspiration Begins in the Garden</h2>
    <p>
      From historic garden traditions to practical planting
      advice, gardening offers endless opportunities to learn,
      create, and enjoy the natural world.
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .garden-intro {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .garden-intro > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.85;
  }

  .garden-nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: .65rem;
    margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .garden-nav a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: .5rem .9rem;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 20px;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    font-size: .9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .garden-nav a:hover {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .garden-section {
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 12px rgba(90, 50, 65, .04);
    scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .garden-section h2,
  .garden-closing h2 {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    margin-top: .25rem;
  }

  .garden-section > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    line-height: 1.85;
  }

  .garden-feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .garden-feature {
    padding: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .garden-feature h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
  }

  .garden-feature p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .garden-list {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .garden-link {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .garden-link a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: .7rem 1.2rem;
    background: var(--accent-dark);
    color: #ffffff;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .garden-link a:hover {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .garden-closing {
    margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }

  .garden-closing p:last-child {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.85;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .garden-section {
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .garden-feature-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .garden-nav {
      gap: .5rem;
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .garden-nav a {
      font-size: .85rem;
    }

    .garden-closing {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
